      "name": "Code change and review",
      "summary": "Getting a change to the PLATFORM from \"this is needed\" to merged: claim the work, branch and announce it, make the change, prove it against the platform's own gates, and carry it through review to a merge somebody else is not left holding.",
      "description": "Getting a change to the PLATFORM from \"this is needed\" to merged: claim the work, branch and announce it, make the change, prove it against the platform's own gates, and carry it through review to a merge somebody else is not left holding.\n\nYou are in this process for a change to folio-assistant itself. `content-change-review` is the same shape for a folio's content, and the acceptance differs: here a code reviewer judges the engineering, there a review committee judges the editorial.\n\nThe loop back through \"root-cause the failure\" is the point of drawing this at all. Red CI is not a state you report and leave; it is a state you re-enter the process from. The same is true of a review that is not clear.",
      "enforcement": "strict",
      "sourcePath": "processes/sdlc/code-change-review.bpmn",
